INT. FAMILY DINING ROOM - SUNDAY

A long table. Plates of roast. A cuckoo clock. Gravy steams.

GRANDPA WILF, eighty, at the head. KATARZYNA, forties, carves. SIONE, forties, pours wine. The twins, PEACHES and BO, seven, kick each other under the table.

PEACHES
Bo took my potato!

BO
You took mine first!

SIONE
Both of you, hands where I can see them.

KATARZYNA
(to the room)
Eat, everybody. It's getting cold.

WILF
(muttering)
Everything's cold in this house.

KATARZYNA
I heard that, Wilf.

WILF
Good.

SIONE
Peaches, give Bo the potato.

PEACHES
No!

BO
Mom!

KATARZYNA
Stop. Both of you.

They stop. Silence. The clock cuckoos twice.

WILF
Well. Anybody going to tell the children?

KATARZYNA and SIONE look at each other.

SIONE
Wilf.

WILF
It's Sunday. They should know.

BO
Know what?

KATARZYNA
(gently)
Grandpa's moving in next month.

PEACHES
Forever?

WILF
Till they carry me out.

Peaches considers this with great gravity, then slides her potato across the table to Bo.
